IO-Tty 1.12 and older do not build on EL8 or newer. Makefile.PL probes each pty
function by compiling a program that only takes its address; the current
toolchain drops that reference, so the probe reports _getpty as present, the
build defines HAVE__GETPTY, and IO/Tty/Tty.so then fails to load with
"undefined symbol: _getpty". IO-Tty 1.20 calls the function in the probe, so
the link fails and the probe answers correctly.

Source: https://cpan.metacpan.org/authors/id/T/TO/TODDR/IO-Tty-1.20.tar.gz

xcat-dep ships IO-Tty 1.20-1. EL8 PowerTools carries 1.12-11 and EL9 CRB carries
1.16-4, so the xcat-dep rpm outranks the distribution copy on a management node
that enables those repositories. Both distribution builds load correctly; they
are shadowed because a service node reads no CRB and one repository serves both
roles. 1.20 is the same upstream release the distributions package, with the same
license, the same vendor paths and the same perl(IO::Tty) provides, so the higher
version is an upgrade and not a fork. EL10 CRB carries 1.20-7, which outranks
1.20-1, so the distribution copy still wins there.
